 "path": "memory/continual-arc-diagonal-ray.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern: extend diagonal rays\n\nObserved in task-db7b98a6 (solved): when a non-background color has a diagonal sequence of cells, continue the same-color diagonal ray through background cells to the grid edge(s), preserving original cells and other colors. The continuation may extend from both ends of a diagonal line. Don't overwrite cells occupied by other colors. Examples across demonstrations: diagonal 0 / 4 / 9 / 7 rays were prolonged along their slope; test had 4s on a down-left diagonal (r2c13, r3c12, r4c11, r5c10 in 1-based indexing), so extend that ray to r1c14 and r6c9, r7c8, r8c7. The small 1 diagonal was not extended; the target line was the longer repeated color-4 ray. This is evidence from one task family, not a universal ARC rule.\n"
